        "message": "LU-21092 gss: make lgssc an internal key type\n\nKeys of the lgssc type are only meant to be requested when it needs\na new GSS context. Prefix the key type name with a dot, so that the\nkeys subsystem handles it as an internal key type, and update the\nrequest-key rule accordingly.\n\nrequest-key from keyutils before 1.6 only opens\n/etc/request-key.d/<key type>.conf. keyutils 1.6 and later read every\n*.conf file in request-key.d and match the key type inside the rule,\nbut skip file names starting with a dot. So make lgssc.conf the rule\nfile, and add a .lgssc.conf symlink to it, for older keyutils. Newer\nkeyutils ignore the symlink, so the rule is never matched twice.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: kerberos=true testlist=sanity-krb5 clientdistro=el8.10 serverdistro=el8.10\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1 clientdistro=el8.10 serverdistro=el8.10\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2 clientdistro=el8.10 serverdistro=el8.10\nTest-Parameters: kerberos=true testlist=sanity-krb5 clientdistro=el9.7 serverdistro=el9.7\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1 clientdistro=el9.7 serverdistro=el9.7\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2 clientdistro=el9.7 serverdistro=el9.7\nTest-Parameters: kerberos=true testlist=sanity-krb5 clientdistro=el10.2 serverdistro=el10.2\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1 clientdistro=el10.2 serverdistro=el10.2\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2 clientdistro=el10.2 serverdistro=el10.2\nSigned-off-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I471e9b2cdd31879209e881f40b035be032dbefee\n"
      },
